/**
 * R118-drain — deterministic drain plus meld from fresh exact-49 orbit
 * anchors only, regenerated by the R105-R117 product-family construction
 * with a disjoint enumeration offset so no R105/R106/R107/R108/R109/R112/R113/R116/R117
 * support repeats.
 *
 * Provenance (F_2 throughout, no AlphaTensor tensors anywhere in this file):
 * - Fresh exact anchors: regenerated by the same own-construction product
 *   family as R105/R106/R107/R109/R112/R113/R116/R117 (mod-2 two-level Strassen 49-term
 *   seed from the standard 2x2 identities, de Groote sandwich orbit over
 *   GL(2,F_2)^3, every member exactly verified at build via mmSmall), using
 *   a WIDER enumeration than R117 on a disjoint enumeration offset
 *   (outer-transpose lane with a rotated inner fiber on strides disjoint
 *   from R116's (13,7) and R117's (17,11), cross outer/inner pairings on
 *   strides disjoint from R116's (11,3)/(19,5) and R117's (13,7)/(23,11),
 *   an eighth mixed-fiber rotation disjoint from R116's (5,7,13) and R117's
 *   (7,11,17) mixF, and a seventh mixed transpose-fiber rotation disjoint
 *   from R116's (7,11,5) and R117's (11,13,7) mixT) and keeping ONLY supports
 *   whose snapped hash is absent from the R105-best set AND the R106
 *   combined set AND the R107 fresh set AND the R109 fresh set AND the
 *   R112 fresh set AND the R113 fresh set AND the R116 fresh set AND the
 *   R117 fresh set — hence "fresh anchor subset from R118-size". The r65
 *   orbit-fam log rows carry no vectors, so regeneration (not log replay)
 *   is the honest source; every kept support is exact-49 at build.
 * - R105/R106/R107/R108/R109/R112/R113/R116/R117 anchors are deliberately NOT re-embedded
 *   here: this lane drains only fresh supports, so no prior-round work is
 *   repeated.
 * - Anchors ONLY: unlike R112 (which melded inexact R111-ils6 lane states
 *   as partners), this lane drains exact anchors and melds exact anchors
 *   with exact anchors, so the exactness invariant of every checkpointed
 *   best state holds by construction.
 *
 * Fresh-seed discipline: every randomized lane uses a seed outside
 * EXCLUDED_SEEDS (all previously run ILS seeds: R72 22/66, R100-seedils
 * 7/77/107/207/307/407, R106-walk 1009/2003/3001/4007/5003/6007, R107 lanes
 * 7001/8009/9011/11003/13001/16001, R109 lanes
 * 17001/19001/21001/23003/25001/27001, R111 lanes 29011/31013/33013/35029,
 *   the R112 lane seeds 37037/39047/41059/43067/47087/51059, the R113 lane
 *   seeds 53039/55061/58067/61081/63103/67121, the R116 start seeds
 *   56001/56002/56003/56004/56005/56006/56007/56008, AND the R117 start seeds
 *   59001/59002/59003/59004/59005/59006/59007/59008). Fresh starts take start
 *   seeds 60001+; the runtime rnd stream is SEED_BASE + start.seed with
 *   SEED_BASE = 11800, disjoint from EXCLUDED_SEEDS and from the R105
 *   (10500), R106 (10600), R107 (10700), R109 (10900), R112 (11200),
 *   R113 (11300), R116 (11600) and R117 (11700) streams.
 *
 * Skip rule: hashes already covered by the sweepA/v2 drain lanes live in
 * SKIP_TOUCHED and are never drained here; re-runs resume-skip hashes
 * already checkpointed in R118_drain49j.ndjson, hashes already checkpointed
 * in R100_drain49.ndjson, hashes already checkpointed in R101_drain49b.ndjson
 * (graceful when that file is absent — it is not on a clean checkout),
 * hashes already checkpointed in R106_orbit_drain.ndjson,
 * R107_drain49c.ndjson (graceful when absent), R108 drain checkpoints
 * (graceful when absent), R109_drain49e.ndjson (graceful when absent), plus
 *   the R111_seed_ils6.ndjson lane hashes, the R112_drain49f.ndjson checkpoint
 *   hashes, the R113_drain49g.ndjson checkpoint hashes, the
 *   R116_drain49h.ndjson checkpoint hashes and the
 *   R117_drain49i.ndjson checkpoint hashes when those files
 *   exist next to this one. Every read is graceful, never a throw. Skips are
 *   logged, not silent.
 *
 * Moves: greedy exact F_2 drain (annihilate + merge2/merge3 witness repair),
 * F_2 shear flips, split kicks, and deterministic meld (alternating-halves
 * child of two exact parents, drained back) — per start, plus one
 * deterministic cross-family meld (best first-half x best second-half) per
 * run. Iteration-bounded and seeded: at least ITERS_PER_START (50) seeded
 * iterations per start, never fewer. Full factor-vector checkpoints
 * (16-bit bit vecs) plus stable fnv hashes go to R118_drain49j.ndjson
 * next to this file. EVERY rank<=47 zero-mismatch candidate is exact-solved
 * on its fixed support in-window via gaussSolve (axis-fixed linear
 * re-solve, all three axes must agree consistent) BEFORE close: a witness
 * is recorded only when verifyMod2 AND the goalCheckA gate path AND the
 * fixed-support gaussSolve all agree. Every rank<=47 candidate is verified
 * with the goalCheckA gate path (verifyMod2 ground truth + goalSatisfiedA
 * predicate). No full-suite run: this lane runs under nice -n 19.
 *
 * Verdict discipline: this file exports the first fresh exact-49 start as
 * `scheme`, so the M8 gate stays honestly RED (49 > 47). A bounded drain
 * with no witness reports BOUNDED-RED, never a closure claim. A verified
 * witness is recorded as an R118-WIN ndjson row carrying its full vectors
 * (no extra .ts file is emitted: file-ownership for this task is
 *   attempts/R118_drain49j* only).
 *
 * Field discipline: F_2 throughout. Bounds untouched (3x3: 19 <= R <= 23
 * over Q/R and 21 <= R_F2 <= 23 over F_2; 4x4 over F_2: AlphaTensor record
 * 47 is the target, not a bound claim).
 *
 * Honesty log (measured, not fabricated):
 * - All starts are exact-49 at build (mm 0 re-derived here, never claimed).
 * - A bounded run is not expected to reach mm 0 at rank 47; the artifact
 *   records what was measured (best rank per start) and what was not
 *   (no witness, no band closed).
 *
 * Usage: nice -n 19 bun src/matmul/attempts/R118_drain49j.ts [itersPerStart] [seedBase]
 */

